# Making

Making is a conceptual tool or principle that helps understand and navigate complex situations. It provides a mental shortcut or framework for making sense of patterns and relationships in the world.^[raw/articles/Making.md]

## Definition
Making functions as a universal mental model with applicability across all domains. It is characterized as a mental shortcut for making sense of patterns and relationships, enabling individuals to navigate complexity through pattern and relationship recognition.^[raw/articles/Making.md]

## Confidence
The confidence level for this model is 0.7, indicating moderate certainty in its distinctiveness and value as a standalone mental model.^[raw/articles/Making.md]

## Connection to Algorithms to Live By
This mental model is explicitly attributed to *Algorithms to Live By* by Brian Christian and Tom Griffiths.^[raw/articles/Making.md] It relates to the broader set of frameworks in that book covering optimization, scheduling, and resource allocation.

